<pdd-dependency>brain/library_index_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/stem_crate.py`. The stem crate. scan(index_path, *, mixxx_db=None, with_mixxx=True) reads available tracks from the library index through a cheap SQL prefilter (title/path/dj_notes containing inst, cap, apel, vocal, karaoke or track_kind=), classifies each with brain.stems.classify_track (hand override, then title tag, then filename, then an exact `instrumental` folder), and keeps vocals-only and instrumental-only rows plus every hand override. BPM, key and length come from Mixxx's own library database (read-only, shared.mixxx_db) when analyzed, else from tags, else None (Mixxx analyzes on load); each row records bpm_source, kind_source, kind_evidence and a clean/radio flag. list_stems(kind=None, *, search='', ...) returns {'vocals_only': [...], 'instrumental_only': [...], 'counts'}; kind accepts vocals/instrumentals aliases; search matches every word of artist/title/album/genre ignoring apostrophes. set_track_kind(track_id, kind, index_path) stores the hand override as `track_kind=<kind>` in the GLOBAL tracks.dj_notes (so rescans and plan overlays keep it; brain.plan_notes carries it), preserving other note text; `auto` removes it. suggest_beds(vocal, rows, *, limit) ranks instrumentals for one vocal: tempo compatibility x3 (half/double allowed), key x2, +0.5 for a different song (a vocal on its own instrumental is just the original record, legal but not preferred). CLI `python -m brain.stem_crate list|set-kind|beds` with --json.

Human story: `user_stories/story__when_i_pick_a_vocal_and_an_instrumental_mixxx_plays_them_together_live.md`; it extends `user_stories/story__when_i_add_vocals_only_and_instrumental_only_tracks_i_layer_them_i_do_not_play_the_acapella_in_full.md`, whose rules (never a dry acapella, the bed stays live, Get Up over Outta Control is the canonical layer) still hold.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Nothing in this module renders audio; Mixxx plays the original files live.
- Target Python 3.13+.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests (`tests/test_stem_layer.py`, `tests/test_stems.py`) before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

The stem crate. scan(index_path, *, mixxx_db=None, with_mixxx=True) reads available tracks from the library index through a cheap SQL prefilter (title/path/dj_notes containing inst, cap, apel, vocal, karaoke or track_kind=), classifies each with brain.stems.classify_track (hand override, then title tag, then filename, then an exact `instrumental` folder), and keeps vocals-only and instrumental-only rows plus every hand override. BPM, key and length come from Mixxx's own library database (read-only, shared.mixxx_db) when analyzed, else from tags, else None (Mixxx analyzes on load); each row records bpm_source, kind_source, kind_evidence and a clean/radio flag. list_stems(kind=None, *, search='', ...) returns {'vocals_only': [...], 'instrumental_only': [...], 'counts'}; kind accepts vocals/instrumentals aliases; search matches every word of artist/title/album/genre ignoring apostrophes. set_track_kind(track_id, kind, index_path) stores the hand override as `track_kind=<kind>` in the GLOBAL tracks.dj_notes (so rescans and plan overlays keep it; brain.plan_notes carries it), preserving other note text; `auto` removes it. suggest_beds(vocal, rows, *, limit) ranks instrumentals for one vocal: tempo compatibility x3 (half/double allowed), key x2, +0.5 for a different song (a vocal on its own instrumental is just the original record, legal but not preferred). CLI `python -m brain.stem_crate list|set-kind|beds` with --json.
